Subject: netfilter: preserve both directions of routed Kite neighbour keys

An inet flowtable installs one rule for each direction.  The previous routed
key augmentation only marked a tuple as Kite when its ingress path was a
station.  The reply tuple enters from the WAN and exits through the station,
so it lost its exact Ethernet key even though the egress endpoint was valid.
Resolve the current tuple's egress neighbour as well, and retain the key when
either side is a Kite path.  This lets PPE construct the reverse downlink
FOE while leaving ordinary routed traffic unchanged.

